00:37:24.549 --> 00:37:25.840
But you can see the difference.

00:37:25.840 --> 00:37:28.800
As a project owner,
I can manipulate

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:32.440
all the instances [INAUDIBLE]
to start or stop them.

00:37:32.440 --> 00:37:35.500
Yet David, as just a
viewer of the project,

00:37:35.500 --> 00:37:36.880
he's not allowed to--

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:40.290
as you can see, he is not
allowed to stop a VM instance

00:37:40.290 --> 00:37:41.120
or start.

00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:42.520
He doesn't have the permission.

00:37:42.520 --> 00:37:44.680
He cannot also SSH into it.

00:37:44.680 --> 00:37:46.300
Again, no permission, right?

00:37:46.300 --> 00:37:48.660
Say there is a situation arises.

00:37:48.660 --> 00:37:52.120
I do need now David to be
able to access into my machine

00:37:52.120 --> 00:37:54.250
to help me
troubleshoot something.

00:37:54.250 --> 00:37:57.150
I can go ahead and set a
policy on the particular VM

00:37:57.150 --> 00:37:59.510
and just copy his username.

00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:00.550
Well, great.

00:38:00.550 --> 00:38:01.960
One, two, three,
four, five, six.

